---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How to Count Words Across All Tabs in Google Docs (2026)"
  description="Google Docs shows word count for one tab only. Learn how to count words across all tabs in Google Docs with a simple workaround."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">Published: October 5, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3">
        How to Count Words Across All Tabs in Google Docs
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
        Google Docs shows word count for the current tab only. If you're working with multiple
        tabs, here's the workaround to get the total count.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Google Docs introduced tabs in 2024, letting you organize long documents into
        separate sections. But there's a catch: the built-in word counter only counts the
        <strong>active tab</strong>, not all tabs combined.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're writing a thesis, a book, or a long report with multiple tabs, you need
        the <strong>total word count</strong> across everything. Here's how to get it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Why Google Docs Doesn't Count All Tabs</h2>
      <p>
        The built-in word count tool (Ctrl + Shift + C) is designed for the current tab
        only. Google Docs treats each tab as a separate document section for counting
        purposes. There is currently no built-in option to count all tabs at once.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Workaround: Combine All Tabs into One</h2>
      <p>
        The easiest way to get a total word count is to combine all tabs into one document.
        Here's how:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Open your Google Doc with multiple tabs.</li>
        <li>Click on the first tab and select all text (Ctrl + A).</li>
        <li>Copy the text (Ctrl + C).</li>
        <li>Open a new blank Google Doc.</li>
        <li>Paste the text (Ctrl + V).</li>
        <li>Repeat for each tab, pasting them one after another in the new document.</li>
        <li>Press <strong>Ctrl + Shift + C</strong> in the new document to see the total word count.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        This works, but it's tedious if you have many tabs. There's a faster way.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Faster Method: Use a Free Online Word Counter</h2>
      <p>
        Instead of opening a new doc, you can copy text from each tab and paste it into our{' '}
        <a href="/tools/word-counter" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
          free Word Counter tool
        </a>. It counts words, characters, sentences, and reading time instantly — no
        signup, no installation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Steps:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Open your Google Doc with multiple tabs.</li>
        <li>For each tab: select all (Ctrl + A), copy (Ctrl + C), then paste into our Word Counter tool.</li>
        <li>After pasting all tabs, the tool shows the total count.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        This method is faster than creating a new doc, and it also gives you character count,
        sentence count, and reading time — useful for writers and students.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Can You Set a Word Count Limit in Google Docs?</h2>
      <p>
        Google Docs does not have a built-in word limit feature. However, you can:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          Enable <strong>"Display word count while typing"</strong> (Tools → Word count) to
          see the count in the bottom-left corner as you write.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use our{' '}
          <a href="/tools/word-counter" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
            Word Counter tool
          </a>{' '}
          as a final check before submitting.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use third-party Google Docs add-ons that offer word limit warnings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Summary</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Google Docs word count only works for the current tab.</li>
        <li>To count all tabs, combine them into one doc or paste them into an online tool.</li>
        <li>Our{' '}
          <a href="/tools/word-counter" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
            free Word Counter
          </a>{' '}
          gives you instant totals — words, characters, sentences, and reading time.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Whether you're writing a multi-tab thesis or a long report, the right tool saves
        time. Bookmark our{' '}
        <a href="/tools/word-counter" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
          Word Counter
        </a>{' '}
        for quick, accurate counts any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <a href="/blog" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
        ← Back to Blog
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>